From 042833743490dbdabb67c23b56201d36ae7fb1a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 22:55:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00361/11171] [outer-loop] Stop tracking large training
 checkpoints (results/**/*.pt); untrack the 765MB exp3734 checkpoint
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The conductor's Thesis-A bounded-training driver saved results/experiment_3734_checkpoint.pt
(765 MB), which exceeds GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit and silently blocked every push to the
canonical GitHub remote for 143 commits — leaving carnot-ebm.org / GitHub Pages stale while
the gitea mirror stayed current. Added results/**/*.pt to .gitignore and untracked the file
(it remains on disk). History purge of the blob follows via git-filter-repo.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .gitignore | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index 342d0e8883..b54fd2fccd 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -77,6 +77,15 @@ models/openai_privacy_filter/
 #   must be tracked (e.g. a small hand-built artifact), add a negation
 #   with `!models/<dirname>/`.
 
+# Large training checkpoints.  The conductor's bounded-training drivers
+# (Thesis-A EBT, etc.) save *.pt checkpoints under results/; one of them
+# (results/experiment_3734_checkpoint.pt, 765 MB) exceeded GitHub's 100 MB
+# limit and silently blocked every push for 143 commits.  History was
+# purged with git-filter-repo 2026-06-03.  These patterns keep checkpoints
+# untracked so it cannot recur.  Result JSON artifacts are still tracked.
+results/**/*.pt
+results/*.pt
+
 # Vivado intermediate / future-build artifacts.  The .gen/ subtree
 # contains >100 MB synthesized netlists (carnot_ising_bd_*_sim_netlist.v
 # and .vhdl) that GitHub also rejected.
-- 
2.55.0

